{
  "id": "valid_boomerang",
  "title": "Valid Boomerang",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Math",
    "Geometry"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given an array <code>points</code> where <code>points[i] = [x<sub>i</sub>, y<sub>i</sub>]</code> represents a point on the <strong>X-Y</strong> plane, return <code>true</code> <em>if these points are a <strong>boomerang</strong></em>.</p> <p>A <strong>boomerang</strong> is a set of three points that are <strong>all distinct</strong> and <strong>not in a straight line</strong>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> points = [[1,1],[2,3],[3,2]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> points = [[1,1],[2,2],[3,3]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>points.length == 3</code></li> <li><code>points[i].length == 2</code></li> <li><code>0 &lt;= x<sub>i</sub>, y<sub>i</sub> &lt;= 100</code></li> </ul>",
  "hints": [
    "3 points form a boomerang if and only if the triangle formed from them has non-zero area."
  ],
  "method": {
    "name": "isBoomerang",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "points",
        "type": "array"
      }
    ]
  },
